<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of Saint Sabas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1256–1270</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of Saint Sabas was a conflict between the Italian maritime republics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, fought mainly in and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> from 1256 to 1258, with fighting elsewhere until 1270. It began over property belonging to the monastery of Saint Sabas and drew the barons and military orders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> in on opposite sides. It weakened the crusader states on the eve of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> advance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-saint-sabas.jpg" alt="War of Saint Sabas" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean &amp;amp; Nathalie · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mar_Saba_(Photo_by_Jean_%26_Nathalie,_2011).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
